t screams \"wrap in this case\" to me."],"path":"benchmarks/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/benchmark/compute/operator/EvalBenchmark.java","id":34952,"created_at":"2025-01-19T16:11:35Z","original_position":38,"side":"RIGHT","position":38,"submitted_on_commit":"2615926608a4ad486e51877de3dd88cf1ef393c1","diff_hunk":"@@ -142,8 +146,34 @@ private static EvalOperator.ExpressionEvaluator evaluator(String operation) {\n                     lhs \u003d new Add(Source.EMPTY, lhs, new Literal(Source.EMPTY, 1L, DataType.LONG));\n                     rhs \u003d new Add(Source.EMPTY, rhs, new Literal(Source.EMPTY, 1L, DataType.LONG));\n                 }\n-                yield EvalMapper.toEvaluator(FOLD_CONTEXT, new Case(Source.EMPTY, condition, List.of(lhs, rhs)), layout(f1, f2))\n-                    .get(driverContext);\n+                EvalOperator.ExpressionEvaluator evaluator \u003d EvalMapper.toEvaluator(\n+                    FOLD_CONTEXT,\n+                    new Case(Source.EMPTY, condition, List.of(lhs, rhs)),\n+                    layout(f1, f2)\n+                ).get(driverContext);\n+                String desc \u003d operation.endsWith(\"lazy\") ? \"CaseLazyEvaluator\" : \"CaseEagerEvaluator\";\n+                if (evaluator.toString().contains(desc) \u003d\u003d false) {\n+                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Evaluator was [\" + evaluator + \"] but expected one containing [\" + desc + \"]\");\n+                }\n+                yield evaluator;\n+            }\n+            case \"coalesce_2_noop\", \"coalesce_2_eager\", \"coalesce_2_lazy\" -\u003e {\n+                FieldAttribute f1 \u003d longField();\n+                FieldAttribute f2 \u003d longField();\n+                Expression lhs \u003d f1;","submitted_line":163},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of eager and lazy evaluators for `Coalesce` operations requires careful consideration. The logic to determine whether to use an eager or lazy evaluator based on the data type seems correct, but it\u0027s crucial to ensure that all possible data types are covered and handled appropriately. Specifically, the `UNSUPPORTED`, `SHORT`, `BYTE`, `DATE_PERIOD`, `OBJECT`, `DOC_DATA_TYPE`, `SOURCE`, `TIME_DURATION`, `FLOAT`, `HALF_FLOAT`, `TSID_DATA_TYPE`, `SCALED_FLOAT`, and `PARTIAL_AGG` types are explicitly marked as unsupported. This decision should be well-documented to ensure that developers understand the rationale behind it.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/nulls/Coalesce.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/nulls/Coalesce.java-6796:6901,6910:7452-7511:8490","promptId":"#7TG7N","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/nulls/Coalesce.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/nulls/Coalesce.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6796,"endPos":6901,"startLine":197,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":197,"endLineOffset":113,"length":106},{"pos":6910,"endPos":7452,"startLine":198,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":212,"endLineOffset":10,"length":543}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":7511,"endPos":8490,"startLine":204,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":214,"endLineOffset":10,"length":980}]},{"id":"benchmarks/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/benchmark/compute/operator/EvalBenchmark.java-benchmarks/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/benchmark/compute/operator/EvalBenchmark.java-6353:6499-6520:6769,6786:6872,6889:7094,7117:7126,7154:7218,7219:8161","promptId":"#PG2FM","srcPath":"benchmarks/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/benchmark/compute/operator/EvalBenchmark.java","dstPath":"benchmarks/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/benchmark/compute/operator/EvalBenchmark.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":6353,"endPos":6499,"startLine":145,"startLineOffset":22,"endLine":146,"endLineOffset":39,"length":147}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":6520,"endPos":6769